$B8C7 ; the shortfall is too big: no robot, nothing spent
$B8CA ; the general resource cannot pay it: no robot
$B8CC ; commit: the copy back to the enemy's resources $FD4A
$B8D4 ; +$0A = $80: an enemy robot
$B8D9 ; place it on the door (x in HL', y in B'): +2 to +4, the cell +0/+1, map bit 6, the radar dot
$B8DD ; the start values; the player's robots get the same at $A6F3, except +6 = 5 there
$B8ED ; order 0: the next visit of this slot chooses one
$B8F5 ; +$0C = 100 (the strength a new robot starts with)
$B8F9 ; no target yet
$B8FD ; the height +9: the sum of the parts' heights
$B904 SpawnHeightLoop
$B90B ; the part heights at $D7B4: bipod 11, tracks 7, anti-grav 8, cannon 6, missiles 6, phasers 7, nuclear 7, electronics 7
$B914 SpawnHeightNext
$B919 ; recount the robots, redraw the status panel
$B920 EnemyReplan ; a live enemy robot: order 0 is replaced at once
$B927 ; any other order is reconsidered once in 32 turns
$B92E ; orders 1-3 (advance, retreat, destroy robots): choose anew
$B932 ; orders 4-8: HL = the target table's +3 bytes, E = the owner bits the order looks for ($B3D5)
