# ---- r5 ----
# r5: $CC00-$D6A7 (construction menu helpers, map lookups, the isometric view, the play screen and status panel,
# printing, the radar, the play interrupt's sound). Evidence: code reading, work/deep/l1.json (call counts, reads /
# writes), memory of the deep recording (frames 18670-18760, 20000) and work/deep/start.bin.
# Entries already in game.ann ($CDD8, $CDF5, $D37C, $D38A, $D3CC, $D3E4, $D42D, $D566, $D59C) get only inner comments.

$CC03 c PrintMenuTotal ; Construction menu: print the total of the costs (the tail of $CBE0)
> Runs after the inline position string at $CBFF ((18,12)): E = $20 (blank leading zeros) and PrintNumber3 prints HL, the sum of the seven MenuResources that $CBE0 added up. 29 runs in the deep recording, one per menu redraw of the resource list.
$CC03 ; blank the leading zeros
$CC05 ; three digits of HL
$CC08 c PrintMenuResource ; Construction menu: print one resource value A at row C, column 13
> Called by $CBE0 for each of the seven MenuResources (rows 9, 11-16). Patches the row byte of the position string after the CALL ($CC11), prints the position, then PrintMenuResourceValue prints A as two digits. Preserves BC, DE, HL (203 calls in the deep recording).
$CC09 ; the row into the string below
$CC10 b MenuResourcePos 4 ; Inline string: position (row patched, column 13)
> PrintInline bytes: 1 Y X with Y written by $CC0A, then 0 (end).
$CC14 c PrintMenuResourceValue ; Construction menu: print A as two digits, registers kept (the tail of $CC08)
$CC18 ; two digits, blank leading zero
$CC1F c ShowRobotDesign ; Construction menu: highlight the chosen parts and draw the robot preview
> IY = the robot record being designed. Paints the attributes of the parts list (columns 16-19, three rows a part, 24 rows from the top): $47 (bright white) for a part chosen in MenuParts, $06 (yellow) otherwise, bit 7 (electronics) at the top. Then clears the view buffer, writes MenuParts to +$07, draws the robot stack into the buffer at map position row 10, column 7 (DrawRobot, base height +$0D = 0) and stores the stack's total height (the sum of the part heights $D7B4) in +$09: the height the ship lands on. Finally copies 4 bytes x 72 lines of the buffer from $6168 (buffer row 82, column 0) to the screen at $48E0 (character row 15, column 0). Called from $C9E7 (7) and $CA0F (22) after each change of the parts.
$CC1F ; the attributes of part row 0 (electronics, bit 7)
$CC28 PartRowLoop ; E = $06: not chosen
$CC2A ; the next part bit into carry, highest first
$CC2E ; chosen: bright white
$CC31 ; 4 cells by 3 rows
$CC35 PartCellLoop
$CC39 ; to the next attribute row (32 - 4)
$CC45 ; empty view buffer
$CC4B ; the robot's parts
$CC4E ; row 10, column 7 of the view
$CC54 ; the stack's height after the last part
$CC57 ; +$09: the robot's height (the landing test adds +$0D)
$CC5A ; 4 bytes, 72 lines
$CC5D ; buffer row 82, column 0
$CC60 ; screen: character row 15, column 0
$CC63 PreviewLineLoop
$CC6B ; the next buffer row (20 bytes in all)
